---
import Article from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site, publisher, disclosure } from '../site.config';
---
<Article
  title="Corrections and removal"
  description="How to tell us about a mistake in a Bolivia Unpacked post, or ask for a correction to operator details that come from the Tourground directory."
  path="/corrections/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Corrections and removal', path: '/corrections/' }]}
  published={site.launchDate}
  reviewed={site.launchDate}
  sources={[]}
  rail={false}
  kicker="Corrections"
>
  <h2>Posts</h2>
  <p>If something in a post is wrong or out of date, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the page address, what is wrong and, if you can, a source. We check the source, correct the post and update its "Updated" date. Health, entry and safety facts also carry a "Last checked" date.</p>
  <h2>Operator details</h2>
  <p>Operator details in the "Plan this trip" box come from the Tourground directory, so they are corrected there and the change reaches this site at the next build. Companies can use the main site's form:</p>
  <p><a href={publisher.correctionUrl}><strong>{disclosure.correctionLinkText}</strong></a></p>
  <h2>Corrections log</h2>
  <p>No corrections have been made since the site launched on {site.launchDate}.</p>
</Article>
